  "caveats": [
    "mv_oberrhein is a real German 20 kV MV network shipped with pandapower (Oberrhein region). Assigning our synthetic sites to its buses is an illustration of the load class, not a claim about a specific project site.",
    "The public case scales its loads to 0.6 of nameplate: 61.86 MW nameplate = 37.12 MW actually served in the power flow.",
    "Violation = bus voltage outside 0.94-1.06 p.u. or any line/transformer above 100% of rating. New loads are constant power with cos(phi)=0.98 and no voltage support.",
    "The two 110/20 kV, 25 MVA transformers are the binding constraint: the feeder's spare capacity is set by them (70.9% and 85.5% loaded at base), not by the 20 kV line ratings.",
    "Headroom per bus is not additive: each bus is tested alone against the shared transformer capacity, so summing per-bus values overstates what the feeder can host at once.",
    "The portfolio snapshot is read from results/loop.json at run time (sha256 prefix in portfolio.sha256); rerun sim/powerflow.py after the agent loop changes the portfolio.",
    "Deterministic on the measured stack (Python 3.9.6, pandapower 3.2.2, numpy 2.0.2, scipy 1.13.1); no network access."
  ]
